      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Baltimore and Potomac Railroad’s Washington Branch opened in July 1872, establishing a Seabrook station that became a local hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seabrook%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1880, a station building and three Gothic cottages stood beside a schoolhouse, marking Seabrook’s early architectural character.",
